  "body": "Release 0.25.0. This minor is BREAKING: the project format moves from v69 to v75 (see `RELEASE_NOTES.md`). Older readers refuse files that use the new formats. Files of v73 and v74 step up.\r\n\r\n## Cut list\r\n\r\nThe maintainer set the cut list. The cut line is 2026-11-21 22:16Z.\r\n\r\n| Item | State |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| #3140 (P1, contour None lead-in) | merged, 2d98d87be |\r\n| #3033 (feat, MCP compact read modes) | merged, ced4dc34e |\r\n| #2920 (P2, breaking, Slot and Trochoidal Slot read DXF chains) | merged, 69c9fd7af |\r\n| #3236 (P1, wire ISO non-finite wire numbers) | merged as PR #3263, 6e1805bfd |\r\n| #2822 (feat, rest machining from the previous operations) | REMOVED: no gate ran on its refresh before the push of this branch. It ships in the next minor. |\r\n\r\nAlways in a cut, without a list entry: PR #3257 (fix for a red `main`, #3256) and the process bumps.\r\n\r\n## Known issues\r\n\r\n- #3264 (P1): the wire ISO post ignores a non-finite `OriginX` or `OriginY` without a warning, so the program is shifted. It was filed after the cut line. Its fix ships in the next minor.\r\n- #1950 (P3) and #2849 (P3): defects with a workaround. The release gate checks their known-fail markers.\r\n\r\n## Decisions taken during the cut (unattended, by the maintainer's order to run the whole cut)\r\n\r\n- The local release package was not built. `cargo xtask release --version 0.25.0 --no-tag --skip-gate --skip-build` made the bump commits (b06e8f5e9 `Cargo.toml`, fe66ffd8f `Cargo.lock`) and then stopped at the `post.exe` check, as expected. Reason: that zip is a hand-test build only; `release.yml` builds the published files from the tag. Dropped: a full release build in a new `target/` during the P1 gates.\r\n- The pixel-snapshot lanes were skipped, by the maintainer's earlier decision that they have no value at a cut.\r\n- The heavy lanes of the P1 floor PRs (#3229, #3137, #3140, #3263) were not run on their PR heads. The maintainer decided that they go to this cut gate.\r\n- #2920 merged on head 638ad26f4 without a third quick gate. Its logic is the same as the gated refresh ea9af2114 (769 steps, 0 failed). The difference in the PR's own files is the formatting of one `matches!` call.\r\n- The second run of `cargo xtask decisions` (for the decision file of PR #3263) added a duplicate `## v0.25.0` heading. It was removed. No old entry of `RECOMMENDED.md` changed (the review found 0 removed lines against `main`).\r\n- Runner failures: a UI test binary that stops in 0-2 s with `exit -1` and no output is a runner failure (#3258). Such a step is run again with `gh run rerun --failed`. Each re-run is recorded below.\r\n\r\n## Release gate\r\n\r\n- Run 44964821090 (`cut.yml`, stage gate), on runner wopr-2: the step \"Release gate tier\" was cancelled at 00:05:41Z, during the first debug build. No test ran. A post-merge run (44964665292, on 6e1805bfd) ran at the same time on runner wopr, which looks like the same host. Classification: runner abort, not a code failure.\r\n- Re-run 1: I cancelled the overlapping post-merge run 44964665292 (the release gate covers that `main` state) and started a new gate: run 44965164703, on runner uma.\r\n- Cancel of run 44965164703 (by the coordinator, 00:10Z): the review of this PR found a blocker (a missing `CHANGELOG.md` row for #2055). The fix needs a push to this branch, and the tag stage refuses a tree that is not the gated tree. So that run could not give a usable result.\r\n- Run 44965350029 (`cut.yml`, stage gate) on head eea778d88, after the fix. It stayed queued: from about 00:13Z no Linux runner was online (the runners API showed cheese, dude, skull, egg, len-pm, uma and wopr-2 offline; wopr has no Linux label). I waited 20 minutes. At 00:33Z still no Linux runner was online, so I cancelled run 44965350029 (reason: no runner exists).\r\n- Fallback (release-cut skill, step 4 item 6): the release gate runs locally, `cargo xtask gate release --no-snapshots` on the exact head eea778d88, on Windows (CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1, CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=18). Result: GREEN. 1333 steps, 0 failed, 122.6 min (gate-logs/release-20261122-003327). The six known-fail tests of #1950 and #2849 were red as expected, and both issues are open. No golden changed. The tree was clean at eea778d88 before and after the run. The tag is then made by hand, under the same empty-diff rule.\r\n\r\n## Process changes\r\n\r\n`PROCESS_VERSION` 101 to 122 since v0.24.0. `RELEASE_NOTES.md` lists them.\r\n\r\nChangelog: none (the rows are in `CHANGELOG.md` on this branch).\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
